 34CL    33S(P,G)                      1983WA27,1977DA02,1977DA03ENSDF    202609
 34CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=LIJIE SUN AND JUN CHEN$CIT=ENSDF$CUT=30-Sep-2026$          
 34CL  H TYP=FUL$AUT=NINEL NICA, BALRAJ SINGH$CIT=NDS 113, 1563 (2012)$         
 34CL2 H CUT=28-May-2012$                                                       
 34CL c  {+33}S+1p|){+34}Cl from J|p=3/2+ {+33}S ground state.                  
 34CL c  1983Wa27: 0.4-2.0-MeV proton beams were provided from the 2.5-MV Van de
 34CL2c  Graaff accelerator at Potchefstroom University, South Africa. The      
 34CL3c  targets were Ag{-2}S (92%-enriched in {+33}S) on Ta backings. |g rays  
 34CL4c  were detected using a NaI detector and two Ge(Li) detectors. Measured  
 34CL5c  E|g, I|g, |g(|q), |s(E{-p}). Deduced reaction Q values, levels, 41     
 34CL6c  resonance strengths, and lifetimes for 17 bound levels using DSAM.     
 34CL c  1977Da02: 1.0-2.0-MeV proton beams were provided from the 4-MV Van de  
 34CL2c  Graaff accelerator at CENBG, France. The targets were Ag{-2}S          
 34CL3c  (92%-enriched in {+33}S) on Au backings. |g rays were detected using a 
 34CL4c  NaI detector and two Ge(Li) detectors. Measured E|g, I|g, and radiative
 34CL5c  capture excitation functions. Deduced reaction Q values, levels, |g-ray
 34CL6c  branching ratios, and lifetimes using DSAM.                            
 34CL c  1977Da03: similar setup as 1977Da02. Protons were detected using four  
 34CL2c  Si(Li) surface barrier detectors. Measured excitation functions for    
 34CL3c  (p,p) elastic scattering. Deduced |g multipole mixing ratios, resonance
 34CL4c  energies, J, and |p from an R-matrix fit on (p,p) excitation functions.
 34CL d
 34CL c  2020Pa40: a 1.072-MeV proton beam was produced from the 5U 5-MV        
 34CL2c  single-ended vertical Pelletron at the Nuclear Science Laboratory of   
 34CL3c  University of Notre Dame. The target was prepared by implanting 70-keV 
 34CL4c  negative {+33}S ions into a tantalum foil. |g rays were detected with  
 34CL5c  the compact detector array GEORGINA consisting of five Ge detectors.   
 34CL6c  Measured E|g, I|g, |g|g-coin. Deduced |g-ray branching ratios for the  
 34CL7c  666-keV level.                                                         
 34CL d
 34CL c  2013Fa10: Direct measurement of the {+33}S(p,|g){+34}Cl reaction in    
 34CL2c  inverse kinematics using 194-514 keV/nucleon {+33}S beams produced from
 34CL3c  the Isotope Separator and ACcelerator (ISAC) radioactive beam facility 
 34CL4c  at TRIUMF . The beams impinged on a windowless gas target of H{-2} gas 
 34CL5c  on the DRAGON (Detector of Recoils And Gammas Of Nuclear reactions)    
 34CL6c  recoil separator. |g rays from radiative captures were detected by 30  
 34CL7c  BGO detectors surrounding the target. Recoil products were separated by
 34CL8c  the DRAGON separator and detected in a double-sided silicon strip      
 34CL9c  detector (DSSSD) at the end. Measured E|g, reaction yields. Discovered 
 34CLAc  two new resonances. Deduced resonance energies (E{-r}) and resonance   
 34CLBc  strengths (|w|g). Summarized in Conference proceedings 2010PaZT.       
 34CL d
 34CL c  2011Fr04: Direct measurement of the {+33}S(p,|g){+34}Cl reaction in    
 34CL2c  normal kinematics using 200-710 keV proton beams provided from a tandem
 34CL3c  Van de Graaff accelerator at the University of Washington. Targets were
 34CL4c  prepared by implanting 45-keV 10{+16} {+33}S ions into oxygen-free     
 34CL5c  high-conductivity copper substrates. |g rays were detected using two   
 34CL6c  HPGe detectors at |+55|', surrounded by plastic scintillators operating
 34CL7c  in anticoincidence mode. Measured E|g and I|g from three resonances.   
 34CL8c  Deduced reaction rates the three resonances, and percentage of decays  
 34CL9c  resulting in {+34}Cl g.s. and {+34m}Cl at 147 keV. Summarized in       
 34CLAc  Conference proceedings 2010PaZT.                                       
 34CL d
 34CL c  1994Li20: {+33}S(p,|g) E=0.973-1.997 MeV, 98%-enriched S target        
 34CL2c  (Ag{-2}S on Ta backing), 22% Ge(Li) (|g rays, 90|' relative to the beam
 34CL3c  direction), NaI (resonance yield) and E-|DE plastic scintillator       
 34CL4c  (resonance yield by positrons of {+34}Cl decay). Enge split-pole proton
 34CL5c  spectrograph with FWHM=200-250 ppm. Studied three resonances. Measured 
 34CL6c  E|g, S(p).                                                             
 34CL c  1992Ka39: {+33}S(p,|g) E=1.8-3.5 MeV, Ag{-2}S target, Ge(Li) and NaI   
 34CL2c  detectors. Measured I|g(|q), deduced M1 resonance. Studied 90          
 34CL3c  resonances.                                                            
 34CL c  1985La16: 1.05-1.98-MeV proton beams from the 2.5-MV Van de Craaff     
 34CL2c  accelerator at the University of Helsinki impinged on {+33}S targets on
 34CL3c  Ta backings. |g rays were detected using two PGT Ge(Li) detectors.     
 34CL4c  Deduced lifetimes for 35 bound levels using DSAM.                      
 34CL c  1984Ke01: 0.82- and 1.43-MeV proton beams from the 2.5-MV Van de Graaff
 34CL2c  accelerator at the University of Helsinki impinged on {+33}S targets on
 34CL3c  Ta backings. |g rays were detected using a PGT Ge(Li) detector. Deduced
 34CL4c  lifetimes for two bound levels using DSAM.                             
 34CL c  1983Ra04: {+33}S(p,|g) E=0.9-1.4 MeV, 88.2%-enriched S target (CdS on  
 34CL2c  carbon backing), NaI detector (|g rays, 90|' relative to the beam      
 34CL3c  direction) and Si surface barrier (proton detector, 135|' relative to  
 34CL4c  the beam direction) proton resolution 300-400 eV. Measured one         
 34CL5c  resonance and deduced S(p)                                             
 34CL c  1973An13: {+33}S(p,|g) E=1.3-1.8 MeV, 76%-enriched S target (Ta        
 34CL2c  backing), Ge(Li) detector placed at 0|' and 90|' relative to beam      
 34CL3c  direction. Measured T{-1/2} by DSAM, J, |p, |g-branching, resonances   
 34CL4c  and strengths. Studied five resonances                                 
 34CL c  1971Hy02: {+33}S(p,|g) E=1058, 1098, 1121 MeV, 84%-enriched S target   
 34CL2c  (Ag backing soldered on brass disk), Ge(Li) and NaI detectors. Measured
 34CL3c  |g(|q), |g-branching, |d, resonance strengths. Studied three resonances
 34CL c  1969Gr29: {+33}S(p,|g) E=1.0-1.3 MeV, 25%-enriched S target (|a|g      
 34CL2c  backing soldered on brass disk). Ge(Li) detector placed at 0|' and     
 34CL3c  115|' or 120|' relative to beam direction. Measured J, |p, |d,         
 34CL4c  |g-branching, T{-1/2} by DSAM. Data for six resonances from 1057 to    
 34CL5c  1266 keV. Studied six resonances                                       
 34CL c  1964Gl04: {+33}S(p,|g) E=0.3-1.3 MeV, 22%-enriched S target (CdS on Cu 
 34CL2c  or Ta backings), NaI detectors at +85|' and -85|' relative to the beam 
 34CL3c  direction. Measured primary and secondary E|g, I|g, |g|g, levels,      
 34CL4c  resonances and resonance strengths for E(p)(lab)=447, 507, 546, 639,   
 34CL5c  662, 683, 731, 777, and 822 keV. For strong primary transitions the    
 34CL6c  branching ratios are in general agreement with Ge data from 1993Wa27   
 34CL7c  with exception of a few cases as noted under comments for relevant |g  
 34CL8c  rays. Studied 22 resonances                                            
 34CL c  Others: 1959Ku79                                                       
 34CL d  ???Added lifetimes from 1985La16, 1984Ke01, 1983Wa27, 1977Da02,        
 34CL2d  1973An13.                                                              
 34CL d  ???Added E(p)(lab) values from 1964Gl04, 1983Wa27, 1973An13, 1977Da02, 
 34CL2d  2013Fa10                                                               
 34CL d  ???Added |w|g values from 1964Gl04, 1983Wa27, 1973An13, 1977Da02,      
 34CL2d  2013Fa10                                                               
 34CL c  (p,|g) bound states and resonances: 1983Wa27, 1977Da02, 1977Da03       
 34CL cG E$Deduced by evaluators from differences of initial and final levels   
 34CL cG RI$Branching ratios are from 1983Wa27 and 1977Da02, unless noted       
 34CL2cG otherwise. For |g rays originating from the bound levels the weighted  
 34CL3cG average is given if the two branching ratios are in agreement, else the
 34CL4cG unweighted average with uncertainty covering both values is given. For 
 34CL5cG |g rays originating from resonances the unweighted average is given    
 34CL6cG with uncertainty of 10% of the value if the branching ratio is greater 
 34CL7cG than 5%, and with uncertainty of 25% if the branching ratio is lower   
 34CL8cG than 5%. For branching ratios measured only by 1977Da02 the uncertainty
 34CL9cG is 10% or 50% for values greater than 5% or lower than 5%,             
 34CLAcG respectively). The branching ratios measured only by 1983Wa27 are given
 34CLBcG with the reported uncertainties (when given).                          
 34CL c  Standard definition of resonance strength                              
 34CL2c  |w|g=(2J{-r}+1)/[(2J{-p}+1)(2J{-T}+1)]|*|G{-|g}|G{-p}/|G, where J{-r}  
 34CL3c  is the spin of the resonance, J{-p}=1/2 is the spin of the proton, and 
 34CL4c  J{-T}=3/2 is the spin of the target {+33}S ground state. The resonance 
 34CL5c  strengths S from the original papers in this dataset are mainly        
 34CL6c  obtained from resonance |g-ray yields and are defined without the      
 34CL7c  (2J{-p}+1)(2J{-T}+1) factor. Therefore, to obtain the standard         
 34CL8c  resonance strength, all the resonance strengths provided in the        
 34CL9c  comments below should be divided by 8.                                 
